# Frontend — Svelte 5 Rules

## Package Versions (pin these)
```json
{
  "svelte": "^5.0.0",
  "@sveltejs/kit": "^2.0.0",
  "@sveltejs/adapter-static": "^3.0.0",
  "vite": "^5.0.0",
  "typescript": "^5.0.0",
  "tailwindcss": "^3.4.0",
  "autoprefixer": "^10.4.0",
  "@dnd-kit/core": "^6.0.0"
}
```

## Build Output
- Must compile to pure static files (HTML + CSS + JS)
- Use `@sveltejs/adapter-static` — no SSR, no Node.js server
- Output directory: `frontend/dist/` (copied to `backend/assets/` by build.rs)
- All API calls go to relative URLs (`/api/...`) — no hardcoded host

## Svelte 5 Rules
- Use **runes** syntax (`$state`, `$derived`, `$effect`, `$props`) — not the old Options API
- Use `$state()` for reactive local state
- Use `$derived()` for computed values, never recompute in templates
- Use `$effect()` sparingly — only for side effects that can't be derived

```svelte
<!-- CORRECT — Svelte 5 runes -->
<script lang="ts">
  let count = $state(0);
  let doubled = $derived(count * 2);
</script>

<!-- WRONG — Svelte 4 syntax, do not use -->
<script>
  export let count = 0;
  $: doubled = count * 2;
</script>
```

## State Management
Use Svelte stores in `src/lib/stores/`:
- `auth.store.ts` — current user, token state
- `board.store.ts` — active board, lists, cards
- `ws.store.ts` — WebSocket connection state
- `notifications.store.ts` — notification list + unread count

Keep stores minimal. Derive what you can. Don't store the same data twice.

## API Layer (`src/lib/api.ts`)
- Single file exporting typed async functions for every API endpoint
- Always use `fetch` with credentials: 'include' (for httpOnly refresh token cookie)
- On 401 response: attempt token refresh, retry once, then redirect to login
- Every API function returns typed data or throws a typed error

```typescript
// Pattern to follow:
export async function getBoard(boardId: string): Promise<Board> {
  const res = await apiFetch(`/api/boards/${boardId}`);
  if (!res.ok) throw new ApiError(res.status, await res.json());
  return res.json();
}
```

## WebSocket (`src/lib/ws.ts`)
- Single WebSocket connection per app session
- Auto-reconnect with exponential backoff (1s, 2s, 4s, 8s, max 30s)
- On reconnect: re-fetch board state to catch any missed events
- Dispatch incoming events to the relevant store

```typescript
// Event handler pattern:
ws.onmessage = (event) => {
  const msg = JSON.parse(event.data);
  switch (msg.type) {
    case 'CARD_MOVED': boardStore.applyCardMove(msg.payload); break;
    case 'CARD_UPDATED': boardStore.applyCardUpdate(msg.payload); break;
    // ...
  }
};
```

## Drag and Drop
- Use `@dnd-kit/core` for drag and drop
- Cards must be draggable between lists and within a list
- Lists must be reorderable horizontally
- On drag end: optimistically update local state, then send API call
- On API failure: revert to previous state and show error toast

## Component Rules
- One component per file
- Components go in `src/lib/components/`
- Name files with PascalCase: `CardModal.svelte`, `KanbanBoard.svelte`
- Props must be typed with TypeScript interfaces
- No inline styles — use Tailwind utility classes only

## Tailwind Rules
- Use Tailwind CSS v3 only
- No custom CSS files except `app.css` for base/reset styles
- Avoid arbitrary values `[...]` unless absolutely necessary
- Color palette: stick to `slate`, `indigo`, `emerald`, `red`, `amber` for consistency

## Key Components to Build
```
components/
├── layout/
│   ├── Navbar.svelte          ← top bar with workspace switcher + notifications
│   └── Sidebar.svelte         ← board list for current workspace
├── board/
│   ├── KanbanBoard.svelte     ← drag-drop lists container
│   ├── KanbanList.svelte      ← single column with cards
│   ├── KanbanCard.svelte      ← card preview (title, avatar, due date, labels)
│   └── ListView.svelte        ← table view of all cards on a board
├── card/
│   ├── CardModal.svelte       ← full card detail overlay
│   ├── CardDescription.svelte ← markdown editor/viewer
│   ├── CardAttachments.svelte ← upload + list attachments
│   ├── CardTimeTracking.svelte← log + show time entries
│   └── CardActivity.svelte    ← comments + activity log
├── ui/
│   ├── Avatar.svelte          ← colored initial avatar
│   ├── Badge.svelte           ← label color chip
│   ├── DatePicker.svelte      ← due date selector
│   ├── Toast.svelte           ← success/error notifications
│   └── Modal.svelte           ← generic modal wrapper
└── notifications/
    └── NotificationBell.svelte
```

## Routing (SvelteKit)
```
routes/
├── +layout.svelte             ← auth guard, navbar, ws connection
├── login/+page.svelte
├── register/+page.svelte
└── [workspaceId]/
    ├── +layout.svelte         ← load workspace, sidebar
    └── [boardId]/
        └── +page.svelte       ← board view (kanban or list toggle)
```

## TypeScript
- Strict mode enabled
- Define all types in `src/lib/types.ts`
- No `any` types — use `unknown` and narrow if needed
- Mirror backend model types exactly

```typescript
// src/lib/types.ts — key types
export interface Card {
  id: string;
  listId: string;
  boardId: string;
  title: string;
  description: string | null;
  position: number;
  dueDate: number | null;  // Unix ms
  assignees: User[];
  labels: Label[];
  createdAt: number;
  updatedAt: number;
}
```

## Error Handling
- Every API call wrapped in try/catch
- Show user-facing errors as toast notifications, not console.error
- Never show raw error messages from server to users
- Loading states: always show skeleton or spinner while fetching
